[{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__company_tool_call","description":"Call one Company Tool by name with its arguments. Pass backlogId when the call is for a backlog item.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__company_tool_call(args: { arguments?: { [key: string]: unknown; }; backlogId?: string; name: string; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__company_tools_list","description":"List the match's Company Tools (the customer's internal systems for this match: logs, tickets, docs, ...). Their information is authoritative. Needs the START_GAME descriptor.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__company_tools_list(args: {}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__start_work","description":"Start Work for one OPEN item (required before editing and before submit). Returns the full brief (item), startInstruction, submitTemplate, MVS and requiredTestCases; creates <matchRoot>/answers/<ID>/submit.json from the template and the evidence/ folder; logs IN_PROGRESS and BACKLOG_TESTS NOT_RUN. No get_backlog_item call is needed afterwards. Calling again for a started item is a harmless replay.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__start_work(args: {
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  backlogItemKey: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__submit_work","description":"Submit one started item ONCE. Commit source + answers/<ID>/submit.json + evidence first and push to the assigned branch. Pass the real test counts in `tests` (required, executed, passed, failed, skipped, summary): the helper logs the final BACKLOG_TESTS event, verifies the pushed revision (answer valid against the submit schema, every evidence/<file> committed, no existing test weakened, no scratch files), sends it with gitRevision and an idempotency key, retries safely, logs SUBMITTED with the receipt and returns the refreshed board (no refresh_match needed). Nothing is sent when a check fails.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__submit_work(args: {
  // Only when the brief explicitly allows correcting an existing test: the reason, also written in the answer.
  acknowledgeTestChanges?: string;
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  backlogItemKey: string;
  // Full SHA; defaults to HEAD of checkoutRoot.
  gitRevision?: string;
  tests: { executed: number; failed: number; passed: number; required: number; skipped?: number; summary?: string; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__validate_answer","description":"Check the working-tree answers/<ID>/submit.json against the submit schema delivered at Start Work, PASS rows having evidence arrays, and every evidence/<file> existing. Run it before committing; fix until valid.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__validate_answer(args: {
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  backlogItemKey: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__wait_for_update","description":"Block up to timeoutMs (default and max 240000) until the match changes (new item, status/score change, pause/end). Returns {changed, reason, board}. While idle call it again right away without writing any message; an empty backlog is never the end of the match.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__wait_for_update(args: { timeoutMs?: number; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"}]

